          "answer": {
           "short": "$y'=2x-3$, for $x\\ne-3$.",
           "worked": "For $x\\ne-3$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{x(x^2-9)}{x+3}\\\\y&=\\frac{x(x-3)(x+3)}{x+3}\\\\y&=x^2-3x\\\\y'&=2x-3\\end{aligned}$$"
          }
