   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p50-quotient-rule-theory",
     "replacement": "For a quotient of two functions $y=\\frac{u}{v}$, where $v\\ne0$, we use the **quotient rule**.\n\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{v\\frac{du}{dx}-u\\frac{dv}{dx}}{v^2}$$\n\n$$y'=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}$$\n\n1. Identify $u$, then find $u'$.\n2. Identify $v$, then find $v'$.\n3. Differentiate using $y'=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}$.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p50-quotient-rule-theory",
     "targetFingerprint": "8d9225133e7e4b2b61650a556c8497cce44d4709aca6340531e6042deec79aa4",
     "applied": true
    }
